Compute Points Above Replacement (PAR) in SGP units
\subsection{Algorithm}{

\code{par()} runs a strict linear 13-step algorithm:
\enumerate{
\item Validate that \code{replacement} carries non-NULL \code{projections} and
\code{config} attributes (abort otherwise).
\item Extract remaining attributes: \code{position_assignments},
\code{replacement$replacement_stats}, and band parameters.
\item Unpack the \code{baseline} list into named overrides for ERA, WHIP, AVG.
\item Call \code{sgp()} on the full player projection pool to produce
\code{sgp_[CAT]} for every player.
\item Build a combined projection frame (players + replacement rows), call
\code{sgp()} on it, and extract the replacement-row SGP values.
\item Validate that player SGP categories match replacement SGP categories.
\item Construct a position x category replacement SGP lookup data frame.
\item Map each player to their replacement SGP row via
\code{match(player_positions, repl_sgp_mat$position)}.
\item Subtract replacement SGP from player SGP (fully vectorized).
\item Compute \code{total_par = rowSums(par_[CAT], na.rm = FALSE)}.
\item Band calibration check: median \code{total_par} of the +/-K band around
the roster boundary must be within \code{boundary_threshold} of 0.
\item Assemble the output data frame (optionally prepend raw SGP columns).
\item Attach output attributes.
}
